# Spring PetClinic — what this repo actually is

Two halves from **different upstream projects**, not one app:

- **Backend**: `spring-petclinic-rest` 3.2.1 (Spring Boot 3.2.1), port **9966**, context path
  **`/petclinic/`**. API base is `http://localhost:9966/petclinic/api`.
- **Frontend**: a 2016 React 15 + TypeScript SPA in `client/`, written against an **older**
  PetClinic API. Runs on port 4444 (`$env:PORT=4444; npm start`).

The frontend does not proxy the API — the backend URL is compiled into the bundle, so every
call is cross-origin.

## ⚠ Destructive endpoint — never call casually

`DELETE /api/pettypes/{id}` **deletes every pet of that type and all their visits**, then
returns `204` as if nothing unusual happened. Verified: deleting type 1 (cat) took the pet count
from 13 to 9. There is no confirmation, no warning in the response, and no recovery — the
in-memory database must be reseeded by restarting the backend. Tracked as `PET-05` / `XC-07`.

## Before you trust a claim

Authoritative, evidence-based documentation lives in `docs/baseline/` — one PRD per slice
(`AUTH-`, `OWN-`, `PET-`, `VIS-`, `VET-` gap IDs), plus `CROSS_CUTTING_BASELINE_PRD.md` (`XC-`)
and `BASELINE_UPDATES_FOR_MODERNIZATION.md` (`B`/`F`). **`ARCHITECTURE.md` carries the map of
the whole set** — start there.

Read the relevant one before concluding something is broken; most "bugs" are already documented
with root causes, workarounds and verified status codes.

## Known-broken endpoints — do not treat as regressions

| Endpoint | Behaviour | Use instead |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}` | always 400 (`B1`) | `GET /pets/{petId}` |
| `PUT /owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}` | 501, unimplemented (`B2`) | `PUT /pets/{petId}` |
| `POST /pets`, `POST /visits` | 400, FK violation (`B3`) | the nested `/owners/...` routes |
| `GET /oops` | in the spec, no controller (`B4`) | — |

Also: **a `400` from this API means almost nothing** — a catch-all advice converts every
exception, including authorization failures and FK violations, into 400 (`XC-01`).

## Working agreements

- **Verify, don't infer.** Run the command or hit the endpoint before reporting a result.
- **Restore the seed data after mutating**: 10 owners (ids 1–10), 13 pets, 6 pet types,
  4 visits, 6 vets, 3 specialties. Restarting the backend reseeds the in-memory database.
- Security is **disabled by default** (`petclinic.security.enable=false`), so the whole API is
  public. Test authorization with `--petclinic.security.enable=true` on a separate port.
